  "WANT: a self-bootstrapping learner that converts one-off warranted functionings into repeatable capabilities — the generative sibling of FutonZero's monitor. The loop: propose a bounded play-out over the capability landscape, predict its field effect, execute only if guardrail-admissible, score the outcome with anti-laundered witness logic, update policy/value estimates, distinguish functioning from capability. Falsifiable: G-SIM (field-simulator adequacy) and G-REWARD (anti-laundered reward) are the two hard gates — until both clear, no autonomous self-play runner.\nHUNGRY-FOR: the Sen distinction made operational (functioning = one play-out lands a fruit; capability = the system learns a policy that clears that class repeatably); anti-laundering (build discharge vs witness discharge — operator approval is a gate, not retroactive proof of fruit); calibration honesty (the forward model's predicted-vs-realised pairs must be independent, not self-referential — the degenerate calibration verdict must not be clearable by more degeneracy).\nHAVE: §4 safe work products all complete — rollout ledger schema (futon0/data/futonzero-rollout-ledger.edn), calibration audit with canonical reader (futon3c.aif.calibration, verdict :insufficient-evidence with ~11+ measured pairs needed), toy field fixture (4-state chain, 18 tests/88 assertions, demonstrates successful update + refusal to learn from laundered reward), policy/value vocabulary (pattern-as-policy + value-estimate shapes, no actuator), reward red-team fixture (8 laundering shapes rejected, 21 tests/127 assertions); the AlphaZero→WM mapping frozen; first non-fallback measured calibration pairs accruing via the WM pilot loop; the two hard gates named with testable clearance criteria.\n",
